    "difficultyReason": "Part a is a direct binomial expansion. Parts b to d add a linear term to or subtract it from the product. The student must bracket the expanded quadratic before subtracting, so every sign in it flips, and part d also has a negative constant inside the product. The hardest demand is controlling signs across two linked steps (expand, then subtract the whole bracket). This is slightly more than the single-step binomial expansions in p21-q1, and below the multi-term, higher-power simplifications in p14-q8-block.",
